          "title": "You'll want to know: le saladier",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le saladier — \"the salad bowl, the mixing bowl\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Elle met la farine dans un grand saladier. She puts the flour in a big bowl."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built on salade."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "saladier is built on salade, which EtymDB traces to Italian salata \"something salted\" (Provençal salada is also proposed), built on Latin sal \"salt\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
